**(2) Substitution.** `BI-2`: `n(ṽ_y) = e_y` — the transverse degree of the boundary vertex carrying a place of `E` at infinity over `∞_{A_F}` equals that place's ramification index. `BI-3`: the local-degree ledger over `p` is exactly `(s_l·mu_l)` and `(e_y)`, summing to `N`. `BI-5`: the marks saturate the non-dicritical `Deg` over `v_0`. `BI-4` places the affine excess (charged `≤ K_p`, rest branch-exchanged). `BI-6` shows DO's repeated coprimality kills are kills of the multiplicity of `E`'s sheets.

